@@ -67,14 +67,67 @@ ## User Administration
 
 ## Queue and Tickets
 
+### Queue
+
+A **queue** belongs to exactly one entity. Attributes:
+
+- **Name** and **slug** — the slug is unique within the entity (`(entity_id, slug)` unique index).
+- **Active flag** (`is_active`, default `true`) — a deactivated queue rejects new ticket
+  issuance; already-issued tickets are unaffected.
+- **Optional i18n labels** (`labels_i18n`, JSON) — localized display names for totem/TV.
+
+Deletion of an entity cascades to its queues, and of a queue to its tickets.
+
 ### Ticket
 
-Unit of service in the queue. It is **single-use** and receives **one single call** — all data is immutable after issuance, except `called_at` and `called_by` (filled when called). Attributes:
+Unit of service in the queue. It is **single-use** and receives **one single call** — all data is immutable after issuance, except the call fields `called_at` and `called_by` (filled when called). Attributes:
 
 - Source queue — the ticket belongs to **one** queue (within the entity); does not record which totem it came from.
+- Display **code** (see below).
 - Priority (numeric, see below).
 - Issuance timestamp (ordering "oldest first" within same priority).
+- Call fields: `called_at` and the attendant (`called_by`) — filled by the single call.
 - Issuance channel: totem, virtual, printed copy, etc.
+- **Status:** `waiting` or `called` only (there is no cancelled status in the MVP; calling is the only transition).
+
+### Ticket Code
+
+The display code makes the ticket visible to the customer on totem/TV:
+
+- Sequence is **per queue**, prefixed `A` with at least 3 digits, zero padded:
+  `A001`, `A002`, … Beyond 999 the code simply grows: `A999` → `A1000`, `A1000` → `A1001`.
+- The code is unique per `(queue_id, code)`.
+- The next code is "**last valid code + 1**" by insertion order — `A999` then `A1000`
+  yields `A1001` (not string order).
+- **Deleting a ticket does not reuse its number:** after issuing `A001`–`A003` and
+  deleting `A002`, the next issued code is `A004`.
+- **Malformed legacy codes are skipped** when looking for the last valid code
+  (anything not matching `A<digits>`): with only `A-X` present the next is
+  `A001`; with `A001` then `A-X` present the next is `A002`.
+
+### Issuance Rules
+
+- **Inactive queues are rejected** — the queue's `is_active` state is read from the
+  database inside the issuance transaction (the queue row is locked), never from
+  a possibly stale model the caller passed in; a queue deactivated after the
+  caller loaded it is still rejected. Nothing is persisted on rejection.
+- Concurrent issuance is handled by retrying a few times on a unique
+  `(queue_id, code)` collision.
+- New tickets are `waiting`, `issued_at = now()`, channel `virtual` by default,
+  priority `0`. A **negative priority is rejected**.
+- Concurrency of the code sequence is serialized by the queue row lock inside
+  the same transaction.
+
+### Call Rules
+
+- A ticket can be **called exactly once**: calling marks it `called`, records
+  `called_at` and the calling user.
+- **Only members of the ticket's entity may call** the ticket (others get an
+  authorization exception and the ticket stays unchanged).
+- Calling a **non-waiting** (already called) ticket is a logic error and leaves
+  the ticket unchanged.
+- Selection of *which* ticket to call next (priority ordering + fairness) is a
+  separate contract (see "Ordering and Fairness").
 
 ### Priority
 
